{
  "id": "zh-a1-shi-you-zai",
  "category": "Mandarin A1",
  "language": "zh",
  "title": "Being and Having: 是, 有, 在",
  "description": "A 是 B for identity, 在 for where something is, 有 for 'there is' and 'have' — and the word order each needs.",
  "level": "A1",
  "points": [
    {
      "id": "shi",
      "title": "A 是 B: be (nouns only)",
      "summary": "是 (shì) links two nouns: 'A is B'. Adjectives don't use 是 (→ 很).",
      "body": "- 我**是**大学生.\n- ~~我是累~~ ✗ → 我很累.",
      "examples": [
        [
          "{我|wǒ}{是|shì}{大学生|dàxuéshēng}。",
          "I'm a university student."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "zai",
      "title": "Thing + 在 + place: be at",
      "summary": "在 (zài) says where a known thing/person is: thing first, then 在 + place.",
      "body": "- 我的书**在**桌子上.\n- 你的老师**在**哪儿?",
      "examples": [
        [
          "{我|wǒ}{的|de}{书|shū}{在|zài}{桌子|zhuōzi}{上|shang}。",
          "My book is on the table."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "you",
      "title": "Place + 有 + thing: there is",
      "summary": "有 (yǒu) says what exists somewhere: place first, then 有 + thing (usually something new / indefinite).",
      "body": "- 桌子上**有**一本书 (There's a book on the table).\n- 学校旁边**有**一个公园.\n- Negative: 没有.",
      "examples": [
        [
          "{学校|xuéxiào}{旁边|pángbiān}{有|yǒu}{一个|yí ge}{公园|gōngyuán}。",
          "There's a park next to the school."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "youposs",
      "title": "Subject + 有 + object: have",
      "summary": "有 also means 'have'. Negative: 没有.",
      "body": "- 他**有**两个孩子.\n- 我**没有**钱.",
      "examples": [
        [
          "{他|tā}{有|yǒu}{两|liǎng}{个|ge}{孩子|háizi}。",
          "He has two children."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
